# Durkwood Boars (4/4, no keywords) is gang-blocked by Elvish Archers (2/1,
# First Strike) and Devoted Hero (1/2, no first strike) -- neither existing
# first-strike fixture nor the existing gang-block fixture combines the two:
# one blocker in the gang deals damage a step early, the other does not, and
# both still have to be alive and both still have to be offered to
# AssignCombatDamage in the regular step (dealsInStep, combatdamage.go).
#
# First strike step: Archers deals its 2 power to the Boars (dealsInStep
# true for a first striker, false for the Boars and for Devoted Hero) -- the
# Boars take 2, well short of lethal on 4 toughness, and nothing dies yet:
# nothing has touched Archers or Devoted Hero at this point.
#
# Regular step: the Boars deal all 4 power, split by AssignCombatDamage
# across both still-live blockers -- 1 to Archers (lethal, 1 toughness) and
# 3 to Devoted Hero (lethal, 2 toughness, 1 wasted, no trample to carry it).
# Archers does not deal damage again (dealsInStep is false for a plain first
# striker in the regular step); Devoted Hero deals its 1 power back. The
# Boars end the exchange with 2+1=3 damage marked, short of their 4
# toughness -- survives. Both blockers, lethally damaged in the same pass,
# die to the same state-based-action check.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks 2=1,3=1
declareblockers
advance
firststrikedamage
advance
queue damage 2=1,3=3
combatdamage
# One more advance for the state-based-action check that moves both
# lethally damaged blockers to the graveyard.
advance
